BT /F1 10 Tf 0.08 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 57 666.0 Tm (Format-specific field names and meanings are summarised below; where applicable the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.08 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 57 648.0 Tm (original specification defines exact endianness, offsets, checksums and format-revision) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.08 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 57 630.0 Tm (limits.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.08 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 57 600.0 Tm (1. BPB_BytsPerSec: logical sector size, required for every offset calculation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.08 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 57 570.0 Tm (2. BPB_SecPerClus: power-of-two sectors in a data cluster.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.08 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 57 540.0 Tm (3. BPB_RsvdSecCnt: extent of the region before the first FAT.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.08 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 57 510.0 Tm (4. BPB_NumFATs: number of FAT copies, not a transactional journal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.08 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 57 480.0 Tm (5. BPB_RootEntCnt: fixed-size root directory capacity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.08 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 57 450.0 Tm (6. BPB_FATSz16: sector count of each FAT12 table.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.08 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 57 420.0 Tm (7. Cluster entry n: floor\(3*n/2\) packed byte offset, selecting 12-bit half.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 0.08 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 57 390.0 Tm (8. Directory entry: 32 bytes, short name, attributes, start cluster, size.) Tj ET
